      "content": "Apologies for the confusion. The \"goblins should be happy\" was just a whimsical way to say that the code should work smoothly, but let's get back to the practical side of things. The `ws.Activate` line is meant to ensure that the worksheet is active before you try to manipulate it, but it might not be the solution to the '1004' error.\n\nThe '1004' error usually occurs when there's an issue with the object you're trying to work with. In your case, it could be related to the way you're trying to select and manipulate the worksheet. Let's try a different approach, and I'll keep the goblin theme light-heartedly in mind:\n\nSub ReconcileReport()\n    Dim ws As Worksheet\n    Set ws = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"Monthly_Recon\")\n    \n    ws.Range(\"A1\").Value = \"Date\"\n    ws.Range(\"B1\").Value = \"Amount\"\n    \n    ' This part is where it keeps crashing\n    ws.Activate ' Make sure the worksheet is active, like waking up a sleepy goblin\n    ws.Range(\"C1:C100\").SpecialCells(xlCellTypeBlanks).Value = 0\n    \n    MsgBox \"Done!\"\nEnd Sub",
